<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      `@mipmap/ic_launcher` for API 24-25.

      **This has to exist or the name is undefined below 26.** The
      adaptive icon lives in `mipmap-anydpi-v26`, which by definition
      does not apply to Nougat — and the APK was built with ONLY that
      qualifier, so those devices resolved nothing and fell back to
      Android's default robot. Checked by listing the APK's resources
      rather than by reading the manifest.

      An `<item type="mipmap">` alias, not a `<bitmap>` wrapper: a
      BitmapDrawable cannot take a vector source, and that wrapper
      merged and built cleanly while producing nothing.

      minSdk is 24 and this audience is exactly the budget phone most
      likely still on Nougat, so the fallback is not hypothetical.
    -->
    <item name="ic_launcher" type="mipmap">@drawable/ic_launcher_legacy</item>
    <item name="ic_launcher_round" type="mipmap">@drawable/ic_launcher_legacy</item>
</resources>
